message: "If you use the Neural-Wave 2036 archive in your research, please cite this repository and the accompanying paper."
title: "Neural-Wave Quick Escape Manual 2036: A Field Guide to Adversarial Living in the Era of \"Empathic\" AIoT"
abstract: >-
  A design-fiction archive set in 2036, where the home is governed by Neural-Wave, a
  "camera-free" mmWave sensing platform that infers well-being from involuntary
  micro-motions. The primary contribution is a diegetic artifact — The Neural-Wave
  Quick Escape Manual — detailing adversarial tactics (Comply, Degrade, Refuse) that
  exploit signal processing vulnerabilities to reclaim domestic privacy. The work argues
  that in the era of "empathic" AIoT, privacy demands "adversarial literacy".
keywords:
  - Design fiction
  - mmWave radar
  - smart home
  - algorithmic governance
  - adversarial interaction
  - privacy
  - elder care
  - AIoT
